---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQ - Strata Support">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="support-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/support">Support</a> / FAQ
      </nav>

      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>General</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Is Strata free?</h3>
          <p>Yes, Strata is free forever under the AGPL-3.0-or-later license. There are no subscriptions, no feature lockouts, and no cloud requirements. Download once and own your tools forever.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What platforms does Strata support?</h3>
          <p>Strata supports Linux (x86_64), macOS Universal (Intel + Apple Silicon, 13+), and Windows 10/11 (x86_64). Linux packages include AppImage, deb, rpm, and AUR.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What does AGPL license mean?</h3>
          <p>AGPL-3.0-or-later is a copyleft license. If you distribute a modified version of Strata, you must share your source code under the same license. This ensures derivative works remain free and open. See the <a href="/about/license">license page</a> for details.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Is Strata open source?</h3>
          <p>Yes, Strata is open source under the AGPL-3.0-or-later license. The source code is available on <a href="https://github.com/strata/strata">GitHub</a>. AGPL is a copyleft license, which is different from permissive licenses like MIT or BSD.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>Features & Capabilities</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Does Strata have real-time collaboration?</h3>
          <p>Not yet. Collaboration features are currently UI scaffolding only with no transport or wire protocol. This is planned for future development.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I use Strata for professional print work?</h3>
          <p>Strata has strong type foundations for print production (CMYK, bleed, crop marks, color bars) and PDF export with PDF/X-1a/X-4 support. However, some features like canvas bleed visualization and high-DPI export are still in development. See the <a href="/features/color-effects">Color & Effects</a> page for current status.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Does Strata support ARM processors?</h3>
          <p>Strata supports Apple Silicon (ARM) on macOS via Universal binaries. Linux ARM and Windows ARM are not currently supported.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What export formats does Strata support?</h3>
          <p>Strata exports to SVG, React/Tailwind, React/CSS-Modules, Flutter, SwiftUI, and PDF with CMYK support. See the <a href="/features/export">Export & Code Generation</a> page for details.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h2>Development & Community</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Who develops Strata?</h3>
          <p>Strata is built by one designer-developer independently. See the <a href="/about">About page</a> for the full story.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How can I contribute?</h3>
          <p>You can contribute code, documentation, testing, design, or translations. See the <a href="/contribute">contribution guidelines</a> for details. Non-financial contributions are equally valuable to financial support.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How can I support the project financially?</h3>
          <p>Strata accepts financial support via GitHub Sponsors. See the <a href="/support-project">Support Project</a> page for sponsorship tiers and what support enables.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What's the response time for support?</h3>
          <p>As a solo-developer project, I review issues within 1 week. Critical bugs are prioritized. For faster responses, community forums (GitHub Discussions) are recommended.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-cta">
        <h2>Still have questions?</h2>
        <p>Check the <a href="/docs">documentation</a> or ask in <a href="https://github.com/strata/strata/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .support-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
  }
  
  .support-page h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }
  
  .faq-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  
  .faq-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }
  
  .faq-item {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-200);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .faq-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }
  
  .faq-item p {
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .faq-item a {
    color: var(--color-teal-600);
  }
  
  .faq-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-200);
  }
  
  .faq-cta h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }
  
  .faq-cta p {
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
  }
</style>
